# Keep the build context free of anything that is not needed to compile, and
# above all of anything secret.
#
# The Dockerfile's builder stage runs `COPY . .`, so every file here would
# otherwise land in a layer. The final image is distroless and copies only the
# two binaries out, but the builder layer still exists in the local cache and is
# pushed whenever a registry cache is configured. A developer who has run the
# daemon in this directory has a real .env sitting next to the Dockerfile, and
# this project has already had one credential reach a place it did not belong
# (docs/discrepancies.md is not the only record worth keeping).

# Credentials — never, under any circumstances.
.env
.env.key
*.pem
*.key

# Local state the daemon writes.
state/
dist/
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Not needed to build, and large.
.git
.github
docs/api-samples
testdata/fuzz
*.pdf

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
